--- !u!114 &1985307248
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1985307245}
  m_Enabled: 0
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.86, g: 0.94, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: a56cf629218f6c947b7f6e013ef9221f, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 23
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "The forward process defines a noisy state: x_t = \u221A\u03B1\u0304_t
    x_0 + \u221A(1\u2212\u03B1\u0304_t)\u03B5, with \u03B5 sampled from a standard
    normal distribution. During training, the model sees x_t, time t, and a digit
    label, then learns to predict \u03B5. Generation starts from Gaussian noise instead
    of a known image and repeatedly uses the predicted noise to estimate a clean
    image and the next state. The changing pictures and values come from this model's
    live GPU textures."
